sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as Citizen / User
    participant UI as :ChatUI
    participant P as :CitationPresenter
    participant A as :Answer
    participant F as :FeedbackLog

    UI->>P: renderSourceCards(answer)
    P->>A: getCitations()
    A-->>P: SourceCitation list (ministry, title, url,<br/>effectiveDate, lastVerifiedDate)
    Note over A: «Information Expert»<br/>The Answer object owns its citations,<br/>so it is asked for them instead of the<br/>presenter digging through other objects
    opt last-verified date is past its review date
        P->>P: markPossiblyOutdated(citation)
    end
    P-->>UI: source cards, visually separate from answer text
    UI-->>U: show "Verified Source" card(s)
    Note over P: «Pure Fabrication, High Cohesion»<br/>Presentation of citations is one focused<br/>responsibility — keeping it out of :ChatUI<br/>and :Answer keeps both cohesive
    U->>UI: selectSourceLink()
    UI-->>U: openOfficialSource(url) in a new tab
    opt user finds the information incorrect
        U->>UI: reportAnswer(answerId, comment)
        UI->>F: recordReport(answerId, citedSourceId, comment)
        F-->>UI: confirmReportReceived()
        UI-->>U: show confirmation
        Note over F: «Creator, Low Coupling»<br/>FeedbackLog stores reports, so it creates<br/>the Report record — the UI only forwards<br/>the event
    end
